# 47 — Prove demanding frontend and backend packs

**Project:** Prove demanding frontend and backend packs

**Goal:** Push frontend-only, backend-only and mixed UI/processing packs to their limits, proving real installation, running, upgrading and rollback under difficult cases.

**Status:** queued

**Owner:** Unassigned

**Estimate:** TBD

**Waiting on:** owner/scope agreement; source and dependency checks

**Start:** [Astrid development skill](../../skills/astrid-dev/SKILL.md) and [shared run contract](../../skills/astrid-dev-shared/run-contract.md). [Inputs](inputs.md) · [Tasks](tasks.md). The [catalog](../index.md) owns priority, status and owner.

**Vision gaps:** [F-004 — Prove demanding frontend and backend packs](../../vision/gaps/F-004-pack-lifecycle.md) (primary).

## Goal and scope

Push frontend-only, backend-only and mixed UI/processing packs to their limits, proving real installation, running, upgrading and rollback under difficult cases.

**Included:** Substantial interactive UI, long-running backend jobs, mixed packs, dependency conflicts, interrupted updates, failed migrations and recovery with real project data.

**Boundary:** Avoid duplicating finished Plan 06; qualify its contract, then file bounded defects and proposed fixes with evidence.

## What this builds on

[Plan 06 pack lifecycle](../06-packs/plan.md), [Plan 17 extension points](../17-vibecomfy-extensibility/plan.md) and [Plan 11 Three.js pack](../11-threejs-pack/plan.md). These are foundations to verify at current source revisions, not proof of a deployed result. Prefer reusing them over inventing another runtime or state owner.

## Proposed sequence

1. Audit existing pack tests and find realistic coverage boundaries.
2. Prepare demanding frontend, backend and combined pack fixtures with pinned dependencies.
3. Verify install, creative use, upgrade and rollback across specified setups and negative cases.
4. Publish reproducible proof and repair genuine failures without losing user project references.

## Interfaces and handoff

Before product work, pin actual accepted base/donor revisions, implementation owners and dependencies. Consume existing pack/component/project contracts; produce a tested contract or working artifact and link exact product PRs. Never infer authorization from a draft.

## Completion

Publish reproducible proof and repair genuine failures without losing user project references. Record integrated candidate identity, real creator/agent outcomes and meaningful negative cases. Completion does not automatically close the associated vision gap.

**Authorization:** Draft, unassigned, queued. Owner decision and focused checks are required before implementation.
